# Project 1 — Raspberry Pi OS & Ubuntu Server Setup

## Objective

The goal of this project was to establish the base operating-system
environment for my cybersecurity home lab.

The project consisted of:

- Installing Raspberry Pi OS on the Raspberry Pi 5
- Setting up an Ubuntu Server virtual machine
- Configuring the Ubuntu VM to run under QEMU/KVM
- Updating the Ubuntu system
- Verifying network connectivity
- Confirming the environment was ready for future cybersecurity projects

---

## Hardware

- Raspberry Pi 5
- 8 GB RAM
- 120 GB storage

---

## Operating Systems

### Raspberry Pi OS

Raspberry Pi OS was installed directly on the Raspberry Pi and serves
as the primary operating system for the lab host.

### Ubuntu Server

Ubuntu Server was installed as a virtual machine named:

`ubuntu-lab`

The VM runs using:

- QEMU/KVM
- ARM64 / AArch64 architecture

---

## Ubuntu Configuration

After installation, the system was updated using:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y

Network Verification

The following commands were used to verify the system:

hostname
ip addr
ping -c 4 google.com

The hostname confirmed the Ubuntu lab system, the ip addr command
confirmed the network interface configuration, and the ping test
confirmed Internet connectivity.

Verification

The final environment successfully reached the Ubuntu terminal:

damond@ubuntu-lab:~$

The system also reported that no containers required restarting after
the system upgrade.

